# .gitignore for Diabetes_Clinical_Data_Analysis (release rules decided 8 Nov 2026, see docs/PROJECT_PLAN.md §8)
#
# Published: code, tests, the app, the notebook, aggregate reports and figures, the demo-only Logistic Regression, docs.
#
# Kept on this computer only:
# * Row-level data (data/): the raw UCI download, the processed CSVs and the train/test and fold assignments.
#   The raw file is re-downloadable and hash-pinned (docs/DATA_SOURCE.md). The CC BY 4.0 licence would allow
#   redistribution with attribution, but the owner decided not to publish any dataset rows or assignments.
# * Databases, which are rebuilt from the training rows.
# * The research-selected RBF SVM (models/primary_demo_pipeline.*). An RBF SVM stores some of its training records
#   (its support vectors, with their classes) inside the saved file, so the file is not published. The app uses the
#   row-free models/demo_logistic_regression.* instead.
# * Private environment reports and Day 1 working notes: they contain local paths and machine details.
#   They are still listed, with their SHA-256, in reports/sha256_manifest.txt.
# * The archive of earlier file versions (an evidence trail with local paths and row-level files).

# Row-level data and generated databases
/data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Private environment reports and working notes
/reports/00_environment.md
/reports/00_environment_fingerprints.txt
/reports/00_smoke_test.json
/reports/07_correction_verification.md
/reports/07_day1_correction_report.md
/reports/08_day1_final_review.md
/reports/DAY1_SUMMARY.md

# Earlier versions of replaced files
/archive/

# The research-selected RBF SVM and its description (the file stores 127 of the 416 training records)
/models/primary_demo_pipeline.joblib
/models/primary_demo_pipeline.txt

# Python, Jupyter and Streamlit
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Links that the "Help agents write better Streamlit apps" pop-up creates in the project folder when its Install
# button is used. They point into the local Python environment, so they must never be published.
/.agents/skills/
/.claude/skills/

# Environments, secrets, editor and OS files
.venv/
venv/
.env
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
